/** CPE-49 strong-retrofit batch 3 (upgrade to the 4-case standard: Sample + boundary + tricky +
 * stress). Boundary cases are the exact ones from the original seed-cpe49-batch3.ts, re-verified
 * against freshly written reference solutions before trusting them for new tricky/stress.
 *
 * - uva-10038-jolly-jumpers: tricky covers equal adjacent values (diff 0, invalid) and a strictly
 *   increasing run (diffs not covering 1..n-1). Stress is 100 lines at n=3000 (the stated max).
 * - uva-10056-what-is-the-probability: tricky covers p=1.0 (player 1 always wins, others 0) and
 *   N=1000 at the stated upper bound. Stress is 1000 test cases (the stated max S).
 * - uva-10170-the-hotel-with-infinite-rooms: tricky covers the exact day a new group starts vs one
 *   day into it. Stress is 5000 random (S, D) pairs across the full stated range up to ~10^15.
 * - uva-10268-498-bis: tricky covers a degree-0 polynomial (derivative is trivially 0, an edge case
 *   in the "skip the last coefficient" loop) and a value near the stated 2^31 bound. Stress is 5000
 *   pairs with random degree 0-20 and coefficients.
 * - uva-10783-odd-sum: tricky covers a==b (single-value range) and the full stated [0,100] range.
 *   Stress is T=100 (the stated max) random ranges.
 * - uva-12019-doom-s-day-algorithm: tricky feeds every explicitly-stated doomsday anchor date back
 *   in -- all five must independently resolve to Monday (2011's doomsday), a direct consistency
 *   check of the anchor table itself. Stress is 5000 random valid 2011 dates.
 * - uva-272-tex-quotes: tricky covers text with no quotes at all (pure pass-through, including a
 *   period right after a closing quote) and two independent quote pairs on the same line. Stress
 *   is 200 lines with 10 quote pairs each (2000 total).
 * - uva-490-rotating-sentences: verified against the official sample's full 5-line paragraph (not
 *   just the 1-line boundary) byte-for-byte under the judge's actual IGNORE_TRAILING_WS
 *   normalization (apps/judge/src/local/checkers.ts) before trusting the algorithm -- last line
 *   in an input can have its real padding spaces intact from a naive implementation, and per-line
 *   trailing-space normalization is what makes that fine. tricky mixes very different line lengths
 *   (2, 19, 1 chars). Stress is 100 lines of 100 chars each (the stated max scale).
 */
